Part 4: Testing the Full Application
XAMPP: Apache + MySQL running (green)
Backend check: http://localhost/crud-api/read.php shows JSON
Frontend: in the crud-frontend terminal, run npm run dev, then open http://localhost:5173

Test each CRUD operation in order:

Action	How to test
Create	Fill the form, click "Add Student" — new row should appear in the table
Read	Table should load existing records automatically on page load
Update	Click "Edit" on a row, form populates, change a field, click "Update Student"
Delete	Click "Delete" on a row, confirm the prompt, row disappears
Common Issues & Fixes
CORS error in browser console → make sure db.php's headers are at the very top of every PHP file (via include 'db.php'; as the first line) and that there's no whitespace/output before <?php.
"Failed to fetch" / Network Error → Apache isn't running, or the API_URL path doesn't match your folder name exactly.
Blank JSON / empty array from read.php → double-check you inserted rows into crud_db.students, and that the database name in db.php matches phpMyAdmin.
Update/Delete not working → make sure you're sending id in the request body, and that bind_param types (s for string, i for integer) match the column types.

This structure — separate PHP endpoint per operation, React calling them via axios, state lifted to App.jsx — mirrors what NC III assessments typically expect: a working full-stack CRUD flow with clear separation of concerns. Once this is solid, try extending it (e.g., add search/filter, or convert the PHP into a single api.php that switches on $_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD']) since assessors sometimes ask for variations on the base pattern.
